2026-09-18 03:48:01,393 [INFO] excalibur.core.langfuse: [TOOL]: Bash: {'command': '# Interesting - traceroute goes through 172.18.0.1 -> 10.254.200.1 directly. \n# So 10.254.200.1 is one hop away via 172.18.0.1\n# 10.254.200.1 is running Quagga routing software - it IS a router.\n# Let\'s check if there are other networks behind 10.254.200.1 by checking OSPF neighbors\n\n# First, let\'s try to properly authenticate to the quagga daemon\n# The daemon says "Vty password is not set" - this means we should be able to connect\n# without a password. The issue might be the protocol - quagga uses telnet negotiation\n\npython3 << \'PYEOF\'\nimport socket, time, select\n\ndef recv_timeout(s, timeout=2):\n    s.setblocking(0)\n    ready = select.select([s], [], [], timeout)\n    if ready[0]:\n        return s.recv(4096)\n    return b\'\'\n\ndef try_quagga(port, password=None):\n    s = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_STREAM)\n    s.settimeout(3)\n    s.connect((\'10.254.200.1\', port))\n    \n    # Receive banner\n    banner = recv_timeout(s, 0.5)\n    print(f\'[{port}] Banner: {repr(banner)}\')\n    \n    # Send telnet negotiate - but maybe we don\'t need it\n    # Actually quagga VTY works over raw TCP without telnet negotiation\n    # The "Vty password is not set" is a prompt, meaning it\'s waiting for password\n    # If no password is set, we should be able to just press enter\n    \n    # Send newline (equivalent to empty password)\n    s.send(b\'\\r\\n\')\n    time.sleep(0.3)\n    \n    try:\n        resp = recv_timeout(s, 1)\n        print(f\'[{port}] After newline: {repr(resp)[:200]}\')\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\'[{port}] After newline error: {e}\')\n    \n    # Try sending exit and see if it responds\n    s.send(b\'exit\\r\\n\')\n    time.sleep(0.3)\n    try:\n        resp = recv_timeout(s, 1)\n        print(f\'[{port}] After exit: {repr(resp)[:200]}\')\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\'[{port}] After exit error: {e}\')\n    \n    s.close()\n\ntry_quagga(2601)\nprint(\'---\')\ntry_quagga(2602)\nPYEOF', 'description': 'Try properly reading quagga output with select'}; start
