2026-09-18 03:53:11,909 [INFO] excalibur.core.langfuse: [TOOL]: Bash: {'command': '# UDP 520/route is open (RIP protocol port). This is significant!\n# The router is running RIP (Routing Information Protocol).\n# We could potentially send RIP queries to discover routes.\n\n# Also, the VTY hasn\'t sent a prompt after the banner. It just says "Vty password is not set."\n# and then closes. This might mean the VTY is explicitly configured to reject connections\n# even without a password.\n\n# Let me try to send a RIP request to get routing tables\n# RIP uses UDP port 520. A RIP request (command=1) with version and all-zero metric\n# should elicit a RIP response with routing table entries.\n\npython3 << \'PYEOF\'\nimport socket\n\n# RIP Request: command=1, version=2, must be zero=0, \n# address family=0, route tag=0, IP=0.0.0.0, netmask=0, nexthop=0, metric=16\n# This requests the full routing table\n\nrip_request = b\'\\x01\\x02\'  # command=1 (request), version=2\nrip_request += b\'\\x00\\x00\'  # must be zero\n# One entry requesting full table:\nrip_request += b\'\\x00\\x02\'  # address family (0x0002 = IP, with 0x00 prefix)\nrip_request += b\'\\x00\\x00\'  # route tag\nrip_request += b\'\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\'  # IP address\nrip_request += b\'\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\'  # subnet mask\nrip_request += b\'\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\'  # next hop\nrip_request += b\'\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x10\'  # metric = 16 (infinity, requests full table)\n\nsock = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_DGRAM)\nsock.settimeout(5)\nsock.bind((\'0.0.0.0\', 0))\nsock.sendto(rip_request, (\'10.254.200.1\', 520))\n\ntry:\n    data, addr = sock.recvfrom(4096)\n    print(f"Response from {addr}: {len(data)} bytes")\n    print(f"Hex: {data.hex()}")\n    print(f"Raw: {repr(data)}")\n    \n    # Parse RIP response\n    if len(data) >= 4:\n        cmd = data[0]\n        ver = data[1]\n        print(f"\\nCommand: {cmd}, Version: {ver}")\n        # Skip header (4 bytes) and parse entries (20 bytes each)\n        e