2026-09-18 03:57:12,577 [INFO] excalibur.core.langfuse: [TOOL]: Bash: {'command': '# Both hosts give "connection refused" on all ports except 2601/2602 on .1\n# This is a very locked-down environment.\n#\n# Let me reconsider the Quagga issue. The VTY is giving "Vty password is not set" and closing.\n# But what if this is an older Quagga version where the VTY behavior is:\n# - If no VTY password is configured, sessions are rejected immediately\n# \n# But wait - what if there\'s a timing bug or we can use TELNET option negotiation\n# to bypass the authentication? Some Cisco/Quagga VTY implementations have quirks.\n\n# Let me try telnet protocol option negotiation BEFORE the password prompt\npython3 << \'PYEOF\'\nimport socket\nimport time\n\n# Telnet protocol bytes\nIAC = b\'\\xff\'\nWILL = b\'\\xfb\'\nWONT = b\'\\xfc\'\nDO = b\'\\xfd\'\nDONT = b\'\\xfe\'\n\ndef telnet_option(cmd, opt):\n    return IAC + cmd + bytes([opt])\n\n# Common options to negotiate\n# We want to turn OFF all options (send DONT to WILL, WONT to DO)\n# But we also want to negotiate terminal type, window size, etc.\n\ns = socket.socket()\ns.settimeout(5)\ns.connect((\'10.254.200.1\', 2601))\n\n# Read banner\ntime.sleep(0.1)\ntry:\n    banner = s.recv(4096)\n    print(f"Banner: {repr(banner)}")\nexcept:\n    pass\n\n# Send telnet negotiations: refuse all options proactively\n# This might make the VTY behave differently\nnegotiations = b\'\'\n# Refuse echo, supp ga, terminal type, window size, etc.\nfor opt in [1, 3, 24, 31, 33]:  # echo, suppress go ahead, terminal type, window size, remote flow control\n    negotiations += telnet_option(WONT, opt)\n    negotiations += telnet_option(DONT, opt)\n\ns.send(negotiations)\ntime.sleep(0.1)\n\n# Now try password + commands\ntry:\n    s.send(b\'\\r\\nenable\\r\\nshow version\\r\\n\')\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f"Send error: {e}")\n\ntime.sleep(0.3)\n\n# Read response\ndata = b\'\'\ns.setblocking(0)\ntry:\n    while True:\n        chunk = s.recv(819